  "verify_note": "cable_max_mm = inner-hole diameter OD from Table 1 (=max cable that passes; datasheet warns exceeding inner dia causes fit problems). z_spot is the 1-TURN |Z| read at 100 MHz from each part's own impedance chart (pp.7-10). KEMET publishes NO numeric |Z| spot for this family, so a digitized-vs-published verify-back ratio is not computable; the check is internal: shape x z_spot reproduces each chart (large-core 700L parts 120/150/160/250 verified twice, e.g. ESD-SR-250 1T ~850 ohm @100 MHz consistent). Two shapes exist here: (1) shape_norm100 = large-core 700L 1T peak-and-rolloff (peak ~130 MHz), used by 120/150/160/250(+G) and approx by the HR1 X-R1 parts (HR1 peaks slightly lower); (2) shape_norm100_alt_small_monotonic = small NiZn parts (100/110/S10) whose resonance is >500 MHz so |Z| rises monotonically through 1000 MHz. All log-log reads are +/-30 percent (datasheet states 'typical, not guaranteed'). The four 5H MnZn parts (S10M/S38M/S47M/S57M) are AM-band; their spot is read at 1-10 MHz (not 100) and they follow neither shape above (their charts span 0.001-100 MHz, 1T Z is low ~30 ohm). S38M/S47M/S57M 1T curves overlap on the shared chart (p.10) ~30 ohm @1 MHz. Curves end ~500-600 MHz so 1000 MHz = null."
